              "body": "**[SUGGESTION]:** Negative coverage for the OS half of the native-identity guard is dropped\n\nThe rewritten test pins `PATH=\"$scratch/bin:$PATH\"`, so `go env` always reports the owned `windows/amd64` fixture and only the `TUSK_CI_ARCH` operand of the guard at scripts/ci-check.sh:68 is ever falsified (`identity[0] == TUSK_CI_OS` holds trivially as `windows == windows`). The deleted test ran against the ambient `go`, so on the Linux/macOS CI jobs it exercised the OS-mismatch half of that compound comparison. After this change every `TUSK_CI_OS` in the suite equals the fixture's `windows`, so a regression that compares only the architecture (dropping the OS check) would still pass the entire suite. Consider adding a deterministic OS-mismatch negative through an owned fixture override \u2014 e.g. a `FIXTURE_GO_OS`-style knob making the fixture report `linux` with a `Linux` uname while requesting `windows` \u2014 mirroring how `FIXTURE_GO_HOST` and `FIXTURE_UNAME` already isolate the neighboring guards.\n\n---\nReply with `@kilocode-bot fix it` to have Kilo Code address this issue.",
